# Prisma & Database Conventions

## Location

- Schema: `packages/database/prisma/schema.prisma`
- Config: `packages/database/prisma.config.ts`
- Shared client export: `packages/database/src/index.ts`

## Schema rules

- Both sides of every relation must be defined with `@relation`.
- IDs: `@id @default(cuid())` for string IDs.
- Include `createdAt` / `updatedAt` on models.
- Add `@@index` on frequently queried fields.

## All Prisma CLI via Docker

Never run Prisma on the host. Always use the `api` container:

```bash
# Generate client (also runs on api container start)
docker compose exec api pnpm prisma generate --schema=./packages/database/prisma/schema.prisma

# Create migration
docker compose exec api pnpm prisma migrate dev --name <name> --schema=./packages/database/prisma/schema.prisma

# Apply migrations (CI/production)
docker compose exec api pnpm prisma migrate deploy --schema=./packages/database/prisma/schema.prisma

# Open Prisma Studio
docker compose exec api pnpm prisma studio --schema=./packages/database/prisma/schema.prisma
```

## Connection

- From containers: `postgresql://devuser:devpassword@db:5432/calendar_db?schema=public`
- From host tools (e.g. GUI clients): use `localhost:5432` with same credentials.

## After schema changes

1. Create migration via Docker.
2. Regenerate client (`prisma generate`).
3. Rebuild `database` package if types are consumed: `docker compose exec api pnpm --filter database build`.
